  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[
/* f(x) = a(x-h)^2 + k, expanded. h # 0, so the sign error -h is always distinct from h.
   If a < 0 then h > 0, so f'(x) = 2a x - 2a h always has a positive term: a line whose
   terms are all negative prints its first term as -(2*x). */
a: rand_with_prohib(-3, 3, [0]);
h: if a < 0 then rand_with_step(1, 5, 1) else rand_with_prohib(-5, 5, [0]);
k: rand_with_prohib(-9, 9, [0]);
f: expand(a*(x-h)^2 + k);
df: diff(f, x);
/* For the generic-feedback test of the y-coordinate: an offset from k. */
other_k: k+1;

ta1: castext("Differentiate and set the derivative to zero.
`
f'(x) = {#df#}
{#df#} = 0
x = {#h#}
f({#h#}) = {#k#}
`
The coefficient of `x^2` is `{#a#}`, which is [[if test='is(a>0)']]positive, so the stationary point is a minimum[[else]]negative, so the stationary point is a maximum[[/if]].
");
ta2: h;
ta3: k;
ta4: [["a minimum", is(a > 0)], ["a maximum", is(a < 0)]];
    ]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
